{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1407085-advice-on-a-setting-admiral-eustis-military-academy","id":1407085,"title":"Advice on a setting: Admiral Eustis Military Academy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-08T22:43:41-07:00","id":1407085,"title":"Advice on a setting: Admiral Eustis Military Academy","content":"I am planning out a setting for a possible Changeling Chronicle, and a antagonist to go with it. My idea so far is a Military-boarding School named Admiral Eustis Military Academy. Named after a legendary Navy admiral, the school has been around since the late 1800s, Admiral Eustis is notorious among Changelings as a Bastion of Autumn, where many Childlings have met their Undoing over the School's century of existence. The school itself was built to resemble a imposing European castle and faces the seaside at all times, to show off the school's naval heritage.<br /> <br /> The school has gone through many headmasters, with the current being Captain Lester Seville. Captain Seville is a proud Navy man, often putting his medals and accolades on full display for those unfortunate enough to be sent into his office. Lester himself is a stern, no-nonsense man. He has no time for &quot;childish nonsense&quot;, often losing his temper at even the slightest sign of immaturity from his &quot;cadets&quot;. To Changelings, he is a pompous, authoritarian, bully, tyrant, and Autumn Person of the worst type.<br /> <br /> My idea is that the Changeling PC's would have to come to this school to rescue a Childing who recently underwent his Chrysalis within the gloomy halls of this school. I am seeking advice on how to make this Bastion of Autumn a interesting place for PCs to tackle and and on how to make The Captain a interesting Antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-08T23:53:48-07:00","id":1407095,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Headmaster was a notable companion to a Sidhe Lord in his Youth, having himself saved not just his Sidhe Lord but the local Court from some old threat, like a Sea Dragon or Thallain or Dauntain. But when the Sidhe became Undone the Seville unravelled and became more and more banal. Now he is at a precipice of has he done more harm then Good? Some interested parties might want him wacked permanently and the school set ablaze but old friends of his might want to counter that out of respect for his past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}